# 009 — Book Cover Images

## Context

Books in the catalog are currently displayed with a generic icon. When an ISBN is
known, we can fetch a cover image and display it — making the catalog significantly
more visual and useful for a school audience.

This feature downloads cover images at record creation time, caches them locally on
disk (named by ISBN), serves them through a static route, and displays them in both
the detail modal and the card view.

---

## Source: Open Library Covers API

**Why Open Library, not Google Books?**

We tested both APIs against real records from the database and the imported CSV catalog
(5 053 records, 2 282 with an ISBN field):

| Source        | Coverage (DB sample) | Coverage (CSV sample) | Notes                          |
|---------------|---------------------:|----------------------:|--------------------------------|
| Google Books  |                   0% |                    0% | Finds books, but no thumbnails |
| Open Library  |                 ~60% |                  ~28% | No API key, no rate limit      |

Google Books consistently returned books in search results but with no `imageLinks`
field for French editions. Open Library has far better coverage of older French titles.

**API:**

```
GET https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/isbn/{isbn}-M.jpg?default=false
```

- Works with both ISBN-10 and ISBN-13 (dashes stripped)
- `?default=false` → returns HTTP 404 when no cover exists (clean detection, no placeholder image)
- HTTP 200 → real JPEG cover, download and cache
- No API key required, no rate limiting for reasonable use
- Sizes: S (small), M (medium ~130×200px), L (large)

**Validated behavior:**

```
2211056466  → 200  10809b  Stuart Little            (has cover)
9782211066853 → 200   9984b  Petit prince Pouf        (has cover)
2070391981  → 404     13b  Chanson des escargots    (no cover, clean 404)
2884453075  → 404     13b  La rentrée               (no cover, clean 404)
```

ISBNs that are actually ISSNs (periodicals, ~496 records) return 404 gracefully.

